#taxon[Idea]
// #title[Title]

A cartesian decomposition on a finite set $S$ with cardinality $s$ categorifies the idea of a factoring $s$ as a product of two numbers.


There are competing implementations of this idea that disagree on what to do with the empty type
- general cartesian decomposition
- non-degenerate = rectangles
